-- A negative Enum8 is not representable in any unsigned target
Row 1:
──────
enum_uint8:  ᴺᵁᴸᴸ
int_uint8:   ᴺᵁᴸᴸ
enum_uint16: ᴺᵁᴸᴸ
int_uint16:  ᴺᵁᴸᴸ
enum_uint32: ᴺᵁᴸᴸ
int_uint32:  ᴺᵁᴸᴸ
enum_uint64: ᴺᵁᴸᴸ
int_uint64:  ᴺᵁᴸᴸ
-- ... nor in the temporal targets
Row 1:
──────
enum_date:     ᴺᵁᴸᴸ
int_date:      ᴺᵁᴸᴸ
enum_datetime: ᴺᵁᴸᴸ
int_datetime:  ᴺᵁᴸᴸ
-- A wide Enum16 value is not truncated into a narrow target
Row 1:
──────
enum_int8:  ᴺᵁᴸᴸ
int_int8:   ᴺᵁᴸᴸ
enum_uint8: ᴺᵁᴸᴸ
int_uint8:  ᴺᵁᴸᴸ
-- A representable value is still converted, by both functions
Row 1:
──────
enum_or_null: 127
int_or_null:  127
enum_cast:    127
int_cast:     127
-- accurateCast throws where accurateCastOrNull returns NULL
-- accurateCastOrDefault returns the target default, as it does for the integer
0	0
-- plain CAST and toUInt8 keep wrapping the value
255	255
-- a stored column, and a Nullable Enum, behave the same as the literal
neg	\N	\N	\N
zero	0	0	0
high	127	127	127
